WEBVTT

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:06.400
Helmsman's Log,
Stardate 50252.3.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.134
While Voyager takes on supplies,

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.971
Lieutenant Torres and I
are investigating

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.442
some intermittent
sensor readings

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.469
we picked up this morning.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.616
We've been out here
almost five hours

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.248
and we haven't seen any sign
of those energy signatures.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.453
Isn't it time to admit
they were nothing more

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.860
than galactic background noise?

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:32.456
I want to keep looking
a while longer.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.433
Just to be sure.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.460
Aah!

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:37.993
What's wrong?

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.767
Cramp.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.240
Klingon bodies weren't meant
to sit in a cockpit

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.970
for five hours at a stretch.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.740
You have a big dinner date
or something?

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.673
What's that supposed to mean?

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.708
Well, you've been angling
to get back to Voyager

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.652
for about two hours now.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.882
Just thought maybe
there was a reason.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.517
Like Ensign Bristow.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.151
What?

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.957
Well, I've noticed
he's been making any excuse

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.189
to hang around Engineering.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.959
Around you.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.366
Freddy Bristow... is a child.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.369
Oh, really?

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.497
Well, he looks
like a grownup to me.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.202
Tall, good-looking...

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.439
and I hear he plays a mean set
of parrises squares.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.970
I played one game with him
and I whipped him.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.950
Look, he has a crush on me.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.611
I can handle it.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.717
Why are you so interested?

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.553
Oh, I'm just curious...

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.081
how someone with Klingon blood

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:35.993
seems to live the life
of a Tabran monk.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:39.930
Lieutenant, that is none
of your business.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.969
Well, if you ever have
a free evening,

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.734
I have a holodeck program
you might enjoy...

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.639
sailing on Lake Como.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:53.945
I'd rather take my chances
with Freddy Bristow.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.349
Those energy signatures
are back.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.955
We must have crossed
into a tachyon field.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.359
What's that?

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.293
A ship has locked onto our hull.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.728
Why didn't we detect it?

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:14.028
The tachyon field must have
disrupted our sensors.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.802
I'm Lieutenant Tom Paris of...

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:35.462
O soave fanciulla

00:04:35.506 --> 00:04:39.306
O dolce viso

00:04:39.343 --> 00:04:46.112
Di mite circonfuso alba lunar

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:54.324
In terra, vivo ravviso

00:04:54.358 --> 00:05:03.926
II sogno ch'io
vorrei sempre sognar

00:05:04.034 --> 00:05:12.533
Fremon... già nell'anima

00:05:12.576 --> 00:05:15.067
Le dolcezze estreme

00:05:15.112 --> 00:05:19.742
Tu sol commandi, amore...

00:05:19.783 --> 00:05:21.944
Computer, pause playback.

00:05:22.052 --> 00:05:23.952
Excuse me, but your entrance
was early.

00:05:23.988 --> 00:05:25.182
You're rushing the tempo.

00:05:26.991 --> 00:05:28.356
I am not rushing.

00:05:28.392 --> 00:05:31.418
You are lagging behind
like a tired donkey.

00:05:31.462 --> 00:05:32.622
I assure you, I have studied

00:05:32.663 --> 00:05:34.255
the finest recordings
of this opera...

00:05:34.298 --> 00:05:37.131
Caruso and Galli-Curci;
Pavarotti and Freni;

00:05:37.168 --> 00:05:39.762
Soral and T'Penna of Vulcan.

00:05:39.803 --> 00:05:41.065
My tempo is accurate.

00:05:41.105 --> 00:05:46.304
Galli-Curci... Freni...
T'Penna... they are all fallite.

00:05:46.343 --> 00:05:47.901
They are mere dust balls.

00:05:47.945 --> 00:05:49.139
Sono niente!

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.080
They are nothing.

00:05:51.115 --> 00:05:54.243
Giuseppina Pentangeli...
the greatest soprano lirico

00:05:54.285 --> 00:05:57.982
of the 22nd century
transcends them all.

00:05:58.055 --> 00:06:01.081
And conductors
take their tempi from me.

00:06:01.125 --> 00:06:02.524
Capisci?

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.189
In this instance,
they take it from me.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.528
I've programmed
the orchestral playback.

00:06:08.566 --> 00:06:10.898
Who allows you
to make this choice?

00:06:10.935 --> 00:06:12.596
You are an amateur.

00:06:12.636 --> 00:06:14.797
You have no sense of rubato,

00:06:14.838 --> 00:06:19.741
no rallentando... it's like
singing with a computer.

00:06:20.945 --> 00:06:23.209
Madam, I may be an amateur,

00:06:23.247 --> 00:06:24.874
but I'm also known
as a quick study.

00:06:26.083 --> 00:06:27.710
And as I am
in charge of this program,

00:06:27.751 --> 00:06:28.740
you will do it my way.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:31.519
Shall we try it again?

00:06:32.923 --> 00:06:34.447
Computer, start playback.

00:06:37.761 --> 00:06:42.960
O soave fanciulla

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:43.989
O...

00:06:45.002 --> 00:06:46.162
Stop playback.

00:06:47.204 --> 00:06:48.171
What now?

00:06:48.205 --> 00:06:50.139
Non é possibile.

00:06:50.174 --> 00:06:52.540
I couldn't remember the words.

00:06:52.576 --> 00:06:54.669
In all of my career, I have
never forgotten the lyrics.

00:06:54.712 --> 00:06:56.202
This is the difference

00:06:56.247 --> 00:06:58.442
between amateur
and professionali.

00:06:58.482 --> 00:07:00.780
Just a momentary lapse.
No need to overreact.

00:07:00.818 --> 00:07:02.911
Piu cretino non esiste.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.681
This is infuriating!

00:07:04.722 --> 00:07:06.713
I want another partner!

00:07:06.757 --> 00:07:07.883
Lo voglio subito.

00:07:07.925 --> 00:07:10.052
I'm the one who needs
another partner.

00:07:10.094 --> 00:07:12.085
You've got me so upset
I can't sing.

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:13.096
Computer, delete...

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.222
Janeway to the Doctor.

00:07:14.265 --> 00:07:15.664
We have a medical emergency.

00:07:15.699 --> 00:07:17.166
Report to Sick Bay.

00:07:17.201 --> 00:07:18.725
Right away, Captain.

00:07:18.769 --> 00:07:19.929
Addio, madam.

00:07:20.037 --> 00:07:22.096
Next time I'll take my chances
with Maria Callas.

00:07:22.139 --> 00:07:23.663
Computer, delete the diva.

00:07:23.707 --> 00:07:25.698
Imbecille!
Pensa veramente...

00:07:31.749 --> 00:07:34.081
Their nervous systems
suffered trauma

00:07:34.118 --> 00:07:36.450
from some type
of neuroelectric weapon.

00:07:36.487 --> 00:07:38.455
It must have been
extremely painful.

00:07:38.489 --> 00:07:40.218
It certainly was.

00:07:40.257 --> 00:07:41.656
Do you know
why they attacked you?

00:07:41.692 --> 00:07:44.422
No idea. They seemed to be
trying to communicate with us,

00:07:44.461 --> 00:07:45.689
but we couldn't understand them.

00:07:45.729 --> 00:07:47.720
Then they just
lifted their weapons.

00:07:47.765 --> 00:07:49.960
The injuries are treatable.
It shouldn't take long.

00:07:50.034 --> 00:07:51.968
Tuvok, send a message
on all subspace bands.

00:07:52.069 --> 00:07:54.230
I want to find out why
my people were attacked.

00:07:54.271 --> 00:07:55.431
Aye, Captain.

00:07:55.472 --> 00:07:57.406
I'll ask Neelix if he knows
anything about these people.

00:07:57.441 --> 00:07:58.635
Doctor, keep me posted.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:04.914
It would help
if you didn't fidget so much.

00:08:04.948 --> 00:08:06.279
I'm really feeling better.

00:08:06.317 --> 00:08:07.545
Can't I get out of here?

00:08:07.584 --> 00:08:09.245
When you're ready to leave,
I will tell you.

00:08:09.286 --> 00:08:10.514
Doctor,

00:08:10.554 --> 00:08:12.613
Tom doesn't seem to be
responding to the treatment.

00:08:12.656 --> 00:08:13.645
I'll look at him.

00:08:15.959 --> 00:08:17.756
Where's my retinal imager?

00:08:17.795 --> 00:08:19.262
I haven't seen it.

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:26.796
Did you move it
from the instrument tray?

00:08:26.837 --> 00:08:28.498
I haven't been near
the instrument tray.

00:08:33.644 --> 00:08:35.544
I've just had
the most unpleasant encounter

00:08:35.579 --> 00:08:36.944
with a madwoman on the holodeck.

00:08:37.014 --> 00:08:39.380
She must have upset me
more than I realized.

00:08:41.118 --> 00:08:42.415
Lieutenant, you're perfectly
all right.

00:08:42.453 --> 00:08:43.511
What are you still doing here?

00:08:44.521 --> 00:08:45.715
Thank you.

00:08:47.224 --> 00:08:50.216
I think he must have suffered
some very deep tissue damage.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.852
The regenerator isn't helping.

00:08:54.131 --> 00:08:55.598
Doctor?

00:08:55.632 --> 00:08:56.826
Hmm?

00:08:59.069 --> 00:09:01.594
I've made numerous hails
on wide-band subspace.

00:09:01.638 --> 00:09:04.402
The only response has been
a single repeating message.

00:09:07.411 --> 00:09:08.901
What's that?

00:09:08.979 --> 00:09:10.708
I'd guess
it's a language so unlike ours

00:09:10.748 --> 00:09:12.739
that the universal translator
can't interpret it.

00:09:12.783 --> 00:09:14.148
Harry, remodulate
the translator.

00:09:14.184 --> 00:09:17.210
See if we can
decipher those sounds.

00:09:17.254 --> 00:09:18.380
Neelix, what can you tell us?

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:22.416
If these people are
who I think they are,

00:09:22.459 --> 00:09:25.189
I can tell you
this is very bad news.

00:09:25.229 --> 00:09:27.390
I've never actually
encountered them...

00:09:27.431 --> 00:09:31.231
but from what I've heard,
I'm glad I didn't.

00:09:31.268 --> 00:09:33.099
Most ships
that enter their space

00:09:33.137 --> 00:09:34.729
are never heard from again.

00:09:34.772 --> 00:09:38.230
Some have returned with
everyone on board dead.

00:09:38.275 --> 00:09:39.936
They're a complete mystery.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.207
No one knows their name,
how many of them there are,

00:09:43.247 --> 00:09:45.306
what their culture is like.

00:09:45.349 --> 00:09:48.284
Just that they really
don't want people

00:09:48.318 --> 00:09:50.343
violating their territory.

00:09:50.387 --> 00:09:53.618
If this is any indication
of their borders,

00:09:53.657 --> 00:09:56.421
it's a huge area of space...
hundreds of sectors.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.951
If we were to go around it,
it would take months.

00:09:59.029 --> 00:10:00.428
I'd say over 15 months,

00:10:00.464 --> 00:10:03.797
even if we could sustain
maximum warp, which we can't.

00:10:03.834 --> 00:10:05.358
I'm not going to tell this crew

00:10:05.402 --> 00:10:07.734
we're adding another 15 months
to this journey.

00:10:07.771 --> 00:10:09.762
We'll have to find
another option.

00:10:09.807 --> 00:10:12.139
If we are not to go around
their space,

00:10:12.176 --> 00:10:14.872
the only available option
is to go through it.

00:10:16.413 --> 00:10:17.539
Precisely.

00:10:19.783 --> 00:10:20.943
Tom and B'Elanna

00:10:20.984 --> 00:10:23.077
hit a sensor net
as they crossed the border.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.987
We have to figure we'll run
into it when we try to cross,

00:10:26.089 --> 00:10:28.956
but there are ways
around sensor nets.

00:10:28.992 --> 00:10:30.459
They can't possibly
have enough ships

00:10:30.494 --> 00:10:32.485
to patrol a border this size.

00:10:32.529 --> 00:10:34.861
We can probably find
an unguarded section.

00:10:34.898 --> 00:10:36.866
Would it affect your decision
if I pointed out

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.232
that encroaching on the
territory of an alien species

00:10:39.269 --> 00:10:42.397
is prohibited
by Starfleet regulations?

00:10:42.439 --> 00:10:43.963
No, it wouldn't.

00:10:44.007 --> 00:10:48.000
Captain... you have managed
to surprise me.

00:10:48.045 --> 00:10:50.673
We're a long way
from Starfleet, Lieutenant.

00:10:50.714 --> 00:10:52.739
I'm not about to waste 15 months

00:10:52.783 --> 00:10:55.149
because we've run
into a bunch of bullies.

00:10:55.185 --> 00:10:58.018
Sick Bay to Captain Janeway.

00:10:58.055 --> 00:10:59.249
Go ahead, Doctor.

00:10:59.289 --> 00:11:01.951
Please turn to your emergency
medical holographic channel.

00:11:02.025 --> 00:11:04.550
I'm afraid Lieutenant Paris

00:11:04.595 --> 00:11:06.085
suffered
greater neurological damage

00:11:06.129 --> 00:11:07.960
than my initial scan revealed.

00:11:08.031 --> 00:11:11.592
I'm going to have to perform
a motor cortex reconstruction.

00:11:11.635 --> 00:11:13.466
There's no need
to be overly concerned.

00:11:13.504 --> 00:11:15.972
His condition
is not life threatening.

00:11:16.039 --> 00:11:17.472
The procedure is
a relatively simple one

00:11:17.508 --> 00:11:19.601
for a skilled physician.

00:11:19.643 --> 00:11:21.668
Very good, Doctor.
Keep me informed.

00:11:23.347 --> 00:11:26.612
All right. I want a plan
for crossing that border

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:28.880
as quickly
and as quietly as possible.

00:11:28.919 --> 00:11:31.581
We'll reconvene in an hour.
Dismissed.

00:11:36.126 --> 00:11:41.120
O soave fanciulla

00:11:41.164 --> 00:11:42.859
O dolce viso

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:48.167
Di mite circonfuso
alba lunar...

00:11:48.205 --> 00:11:49.331
Doctor...

00:11:49.373 --> 00:11:51.841
I have the cortical analeptics
you asked for.

00:11:51.875 --> 00:11:54.366
Good. Fill the hyposprays.

00:11:54.411 --> 00:11:56.345
We'll begin as soon as
I've finished scrubbing.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:57.972
Did I hear you singing?

00:11:58.015 --> 00:11:59.312
Yes.

00:11:59.349 --> 00:12:01.374
"O soave fanciulla."

00:12:01.418 --> 00:12:02.817
It's an aria from La Bohéme,

00:12:02.853 --> 00:12:05.947
a truly exquisite opera
by Giacomo Puccini,

00:12:06.023 --> 00:12:08.287
a human composer
of the 19th century.

00:12:08.325 --> 00:12:09.849
I didn't realize
you enjoyed music.

00:12:09.893 --> 00:12:12.418
I've recently begun
a thorough study of opera.

00:12:12.462 --> 00:12:15.329
I find it...
quite satisfying,

00:12:15.365 --> 00:12:16.923
but I'm having
difficulty finding

00:12:16.967 --> 00:12:19.094
a holographic partner
for the role of Mimi.

00:12:21.872 --> 00:12:23.897
All the soprani seem to have

00:12:23.941 --> 00:12:25.966
the most
irritating personalities.

00:12:26.043 --> 00:12:28.807
These women are arrogant,
superior, condescending.

00:12:28.845 --> 00:12:31.143
I can't imagine anyone
behaving that way.

00:12:32.316 --> 00:12:33.715
What is it?

00:12:36.153 --> 00:12:37.279
A quiz for you.

00:12:37.321 --> 00:12:39.653
What is the first step
in this procedure?

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.282
Establish the axon connections

00:12:41.325 --> 00:12:43.425
and then test
for synaptic potentials.

00:12:43.558 --> 00:12:46.652
Ah. Quite right. Very good.

00:12:49.964 --> 00:12:51.397
Doctor, what is it?

00:12:55.069 --> 00:12:56.798
We seem to have a small problem.

00:12:56.838 --> 00:13:01.605
I... can't remember
how to perform this operation.

00:13:10.385 --> 00:13:12.546
All right,
I've repaired the damaged

00:13:12.587 --> 00:13:14.885
preganglionic fibers
in the spinal column.

00:13:14.923 --> 00:13:17.357
The final step
is to restore the nerve sheath.

00:13:17.392 --> 00:13:19.257
You'll need
the myelin regenerator.

00:13:21.362 --> 00:13:22.226
What is it?

00:13:22.263 --> 00:13:24.026
He's going
into respiratory arrest.

00:13:25.166 --> 00:13:26.394
What do I do?

00:13:26.434 --> 00:13:28.800
Apply an efferent impulse
to stabilize his motor neurons.

00:13:28.837 --> 00:13:30.395
Apply a... what?

00:13:32.841 --> 00:13:34.399
Vital signs are
returning to normal.

00:13:38.913 --> 00:13:40.710
There... myelin
regeneration is complete.

00:13:40.748 --> 00:13:42.545
What's the synaptic
potential reading?

00:13:47.255 --> 00:13:49.723
Synaptic potentials are...

00:13:49.757 --> 00:13:51.349
normal.

00:13:51.392 --> 00:13:54.190
Autonomic and somatic systems
are functioning.

00:13:55.563 --> 00:13:57.724
Very good, Doctor.

00:13:57.765 --> 00:13:59.164
I think you've done it.

00:14:10.512 --> 00:14:12.844
The EMH database
seems to be experiencing

00:14:12.881 --> 00:14:15.509
a cascading overload
of some kind.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:18.610
Doc's memory circuits
are deteriorating.

00:14:18.653 --> 00:14:19.950
We knew the Doctor
was never designed

00:14:20.021 --> 00:14:22.046
to be up and running
as much as he has been,

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.921
but I thought you programmed
safety buffers,

00:14:23.958 --> 00:14:25.448
so his circuits
wouldn't degrade.

00:14:25.493 --> 00:14:28.724
I did, and I installed them,
but they're breaking down.

00:14:28.763 --> 00:14:30.731
My self-diagnostic routines
have always indicated

00:14:30.765 --> 00:14:32.494
that in the event
of cascade failure,

00:14:32.534 --> 00:14:34.399
I should simply
be reinitialized.

00:14:34.435 --> 00:14:36.562
That would stop the cascade
and allow us to reset

00:14:36.604 --> 00:14:39.402
your database and personality
subroutines, but...

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.907
But what?

00:14:42.277 --> 00:14:44.973
It would restore
the original program...

00:14:45.013 --> 00:14:46.640
reset him to the person he was

00:14:46.681 --> 00:14:48.273
when we first activated him.

00:14:48.316 --> 00:14:49.977
In other words,

00:14:50.051 --> 00:14:52.281
he'd forget everything
that's happened to him

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.548
over the past two years.

00:14:53.588 --> 00:14:55.488
Right.

00:14:55.523 --> 00:14:56.888
Doctor...

00:14:56.925 --> 00:14:58.984
how do you feel about that?

00:15:00.628 --> 00:15:04.325
I... can't say I'd like
to lose the last two years,

00:15:04.365 --> 00:15:07.300
but my primary responsibility
is the health and welfare

00:15:07.335 --> 00:15:08.302
of this crew.

00:15:08.336 --> 00:15:10.133
In my current state,
I am useless to them.

00:15:10.171 --> 00:15:12.162
I believe Lieutenant Torres
should start

00:15:12.206 --> 00:15:14.640
the reinitialization
process immediately.

00:15:14.676 --> 00:15:15.768
No, wait.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.437
Wait, please.

00:15:17.478 --> 00:15:19.776
We can't just treat the Doctor
like he's a computer anymore.

00:15:19.814 --> 00:15:20.940
He's come too far for that.

00:15:21.015 --> 00:15:23.779
Doctor, please,
think about this.

00:15:23.818 --> 00:15:25.410
You'd be losing so much...

00:15:25.453 --> 00:15:26.943
all the relationships
you've developed,

00:15:27.055 --> 00:15:28.454
our friendship,

00:15:28.489 --> 00:15:30.184
your sense of being
a true member of this crew...

00:15:30.224 --> 00:15:31.350
all that would be gone.

00:15:31.392 --> 00:15:34.657
I can't put personal concerns
over those of the crew.

00:15:34.696 --> 00:15:36.630
Look at the experiences
you've had

00:15:36.664 --> 00:15:37.961
since you were activated...

00:15:38.066 --> 00:15:39.226
you've made friends,

00:15:39.267 --> 00:15:40.894
learned how to sing opera,

00:15:40.935 --> 00:15:42.960
you've even fallen in love.

00:15:43.004 --> 00:15:45.871
If you lose those memories,
you won't be the same person.

00:15:47.709 --> 00:15:48.698
You said you don't know

00:15:48.743 --> 00:15:50.608
what's causing
his memory circuits to fail.

00:15:50.645 --> 00:15:52.272
Unfortunately, no.

00:15:52.313 --> 00:15:55.077
So, if you reinitialize without
finding out what's wrong,

00:15:55.116 --> 00:15:56.515
the problem could occur again.

00:15:56.551 --> 00:15:58.451
Well, it's a possibility.

00:15:58.486 --> 00:16:01.046
Isn't it a better plan to look
for the cause of the problem?

00:16:01.089 --> 00:16:02.113
If B'Elanna can find it,

00:16:02.156 --> 00:16:03.885
there may be a less
radical solution.

00:16:03.925 --> 00:16:05.392
Tom Paris is stable.

00:16:05.426 --> 00:16:07.053
He'll be back on duty today.

00:16:07.095 --> 00:16:08.494
There's no medical crisis
at the moment.

00:16:08.529 --> 00:16:11.430
I can certainly handle all
the routine cases in Sick Bay.

00:16:11.466 --> 00:16:13.627
Please, let's
not just erase him

00:16:13.668 --> 00:16:15.966
without trying
to help him first.

00:16:21.643 --> 00:16:25.204
If a crew member came down
with a debilitating illness,

00:16:25.246 --> 00:16:27.271
you'd do everything
in your power

00:16:27.315 --> 00:16:28.839
to make them well again.

00:16:28.883 --> 00:16:31.613
I think we owe you nothing less.

00:16:37.925 --> 00:16:39.187
I'll get started.

00:16:41.829 --> 00:16:43.694
Don't be discouraged.

00:16:43.731 --> 00:16:46.199
I know B'Elanna can find a way.

00:16:52.473 --> 00:16:53.906
Captain?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.475
I think we found it...

00:16:57.512 --> 00:16:59.742
a way to get across the border
without being detected.

00:16:59.781 --> 00:17:01.009
Let's hear it.

00:17:01.049 --> 00:17:04.314
Their sensor net uses a series
of interlaced tachyon beams.

00:17:04.352 --> 00:17:06.320
If we adjust the shields
to refract those beams

00:17:06.354 --> 00:17:09.152
around the ship, we can slip
across without appearing

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:10.384
to have disrupted the net.

00:17:10.425 --> 00:17:11.551
Not bad.

00:17:11.592 --> 00:17:16.291
And we've found that this area
shows no indication of vessels.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:19.128
We can slide through,
go to high warp

00:17:19.167 --> 00:17:21.192
and be through this narrow
section of their territory

00:17:21.235 --> 00:17:22.429
in four days.

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.459
Good work.

00:17:25.873 --> 00:17:29.240
Helm, set a course
for the border.

00:17:29.277 --> 00:17:30.266
Aye, Captain.

00:17:37.218 --> 00:17:38.412
What are you doing now?

00:17:38.453 --> 00:17:40.318
I want to see
if the data corruption

00:17:40.354 --> 00:17:42.379
is affecting
your optical sensors.

00:17:42.423 --> 00:17:44.653
What did that do?

00:17:45.993 --> 00:17:48.052
I-I can't see.
I'm blind!

00:17:48.096 --> 00:17:49.529
All right.

00:17:53.568 --> 00:17:55.695
That is extremely disconcerting.

00:17:55.737 --> 00:17:57.068
Please don't do it again.

00:17:58.806 --> 00:18:00.239
Now what are you doing?

00:18:00.274 --> 00:18:03.038
Attenuating
your force field projectors.

00:18:07.381 --> 00:18:10.441
Doctor, forgive me,
but this is very delicate work.

00:18:10.485 --> 00:18:12.510
Could you please sit
over there for a few minutes?

00:18:14.222 --> 00:18:15.951
How extremely rude.

00:18:18.926 --> 00:18:20.826
May I remind you
that I am, in a way,

00:18:20.862 --> 00:18:23.797
your patient,
who's suffering from an unknown

00:18:23.831 --> 00:18:25.924
and obviously
debilitating condition.

00:18:25.967 --> 00:18:28.561
I would think you'd be a little
more sensitive to my needs.

00:18:28.603 --> 00:18:30.867
You're questioning
my bedside manner?

00:18:33.307 --> 00:18:36.743
The good news
is that your projection system

00:18:36.778 --> 00:18:38.268
doesn't seem to be affected.

00:18:38.312 --> 00:18:42.442
However, I don't know why
your circuits are degrading.

00:18:42.483 --> 00:18:44.314
Then... what do we do now?

00:18:44.352 --> 00:18:46.445
What we do now...

00:18:46.487 --> 00:18:48.887
is get a second opinion.

00:18:48.923 --> 00:18:52.086
I'll transfer you to the
holodeck in a few minutes.

00:18:52.126 --> 00:18:53.184
Wait here.

00:19:03.171 --> 00:19:05.298
Computer, initiate

00:19:05.339 --> 00:19:08.274
Jupiter Station
Diagnostic Program Alpha 1-1.

00:19:08.309 --> 00:19:10.277
The program is activated.

00:19:17.451 --> 00:19:18.816
Computer...

00:19:18.853 --> 00:19:20.844
transfer the program

00:19:20.888 --> 00:19:26.155
for the Emergency Medical
Hologram to Holodeck 2.

00:19:27.528 --> 00:19:29.689
I seem to remember this place.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.061
You should...
this is Jupiter Station,

00:19:31.098 --> 00:19:32.065
where you were created

00:19:32.099 --> 00:19:34.192
and where your database
was written.

00:19:34.235 --> 00:19:37.136
It seems... so long ago.

00:19:37.171 --> 00:19:40.800
This program contains a
sophisticated diagnostic matrix

00:19:40.842 --> 00:19:44.073
specifically created for
the Emergency Medical System.

00:19:44.111 --> 00:19:45.408
That's right.

00:19:45.446 --> 00:19:47.073
I should have remembered that.

00:19:47.114 --> 00:19:48.672
How could I have forgotten?

00:19:48.716 --> 00:19:49.683
I'm going to have to play

00:19:49.717 --> 00:19:50.945
with the systems
for a few minutes.

00:19:51.018 --> 00:19:54.476
I'm not exactly sure how to
access all the subroutines.

00:19:54.522 --> 00:19:56.251
Don't touch that!

00:20:08.502 --> 00:20:09.560
Who are you?

00:20:09.604 --> 00:20:12.198
I'm a holographic re-creation
of Dr. Lewis Zimmerman,

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:14.504
the creator of the Emergency
Medical Hologram.

00:20:14.542 --> 00:20:16.669
You're the diagnostic matrix.

00:20:16.711 --> 00:20:17.769
You might say that.

00:20:17.812 --> 00:20:19.336
Something wrong with your EMH?

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:20.347
Yes.

00:20:20.381 --> 00:20:21.473
I certainly hope
you're going to be able

00:20:21.515 --> 00:20:22.777
to do something
about this annoying problem.

00:20:22.817 --> 00:20:24.444
What's wrong with it?

00:20:24.485 --> 00:20:26.385
He's experiencing
a cascade failure.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.255
His memory circuits
are degrading.

00:20:28.388 --> 00:20:30.356
I was trying to bring
the subroutines on line...

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:32.119
If you don't mind,
I can do it faster.

00:20:34.027 --> 00:20:36.291
I can see where you get
your charming personality.

00:20:36.329 --> 00:20:38.263
Not to mention my hairline.

00:20:38.298 --> 00:20:39.424
Here we are...

00:20:39.466 --> 00:20:42.162
a schematic of the EMH
and its component subroutines.

00:20:42.202 --> 00:20:44.261
Can you determine the
source of the problem?

00:20:44.304 --> 00:20:46.204
This isn't good.

00:20:46.239 --> 00:20:49.436
The EMH has a level-4
memory fragmentation.

00:20:49.476 --> 00:20:50.841
How long has the program
been active?

00:20:50.877 --> 00:20:52.868
I have been active

00:20:52.912 --> 00:20:54.140
for...

00:20:55.615 --> 00:20:57.412
for...

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:58.712
Almost two years.

00:20:58.752 --> 00:21:00.014
Two years?!

00:21:00.086 --> 00:21:01.451
Well, there's your problem.

00:21:01.488 --> 00:21:03.854
This program was developed
as a short-term supplement

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:06.290
to your medical staff...
1,500 hours tops.

00:21:06.326 --> 00:21:07.293
I know.

00:21:07.327 --> 00:21:08.760
I added data compression buffers

00:21:08.795 --> 00:21:10.524
to compensate
for the additional time,

00:21:10.563 --> 00:21:11.962
but they're breaking down.

00:21:12.065 --> 00:21:14.659
The EMH is a highly
sophisticated program.

00:21:14.701 --> 00:21:16.726
You shouldn't go meddling
in its matrix when you

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:17.964
don't know what you're doing.

00:21:20.373 --> 00:21:22.807
Should we shut down
his program then,

00:21:22.842 --> 00:21:24.366
till we figure out
how to fix him?

00:21:24.411 --> 00:21:26.208
At this point,
it doesn't matter.

00:21:26.246 --> 00:21:28.373
With a level-4
memory fragmentation,

00:21:28.415 --> 00:21:30.975
it'll simply continue
to degrade.

00:21:31.084 --> 00:21:32.574
There's only
one course of action...

00:21:32.619 --> 00:21:35.383
a system-wide reinitialization.

00:21:35.422 --> 00:21:36.855
Start over from scratch.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.448
We are aware of that option.

00:21:38.491 --> 00:21:41.324
Would it be possible to expand
his memory circuits instead?

00:21:41.361 --> 00:21:42.385
Of course.

00:21:42.429 --> 00:21:43.555
Schedule it for your next

00:21:43.596 --> 00:21:45.461
maintenance layover
at McKinley Station.

00:21:45.498 --> 00:21:46.931
I'm afraid that isn't possible.

00:21:46.966 --> 00:21:49.457
We're thousands of light-years
from Federation space.

00:21:49.502 --> 00:21:51.629
Well, there's
nothing more I can do.

00:21:51.671 --> 00:21:54.333
Either reinitialize it,
or live with the knowledge

00:21:54.374 --> 00:21:56.467
that eventually
this EMH will end up

00:21:56.509 --> 00:21:58.807
with the intellectual capacity
of a parsnip.

00:21:58.845 --> 00:21:59.834
What are you saying?

00:21:59.879 --> 00:22:01.073
Bridge to Torres.

00:22:01.114 --> 00:22:02.911
I'm here, Captain.

00:22:02.949 --> 00:22:04.314
We're approaching the border.

00:22:04.351 --> 00:22:05.716
We need your help
in Engineering.

00:22:05.752 --> 00:22:07.617
I'm on my way.

00:22:07.654 --> 00:22:10.122
Doctor... Zimmerman...

00:22:10.156 --> 00:22:12.590
you haven't told us anything
that we don't already know.

00:22:12.625 --> 00:22:13.956
What I need is to find out

00:22:13.993 --> 00:22:16.791
exactly why the Doctor's
memory circuits are degrading

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:18.798
so that we can come up
with a solution.

00:22:18.832 --> 00:22:20.800
Activate a level-4 diagnostic,

00:22:20.834 --> 00:22:22.631
or whatever you need to do
to get us some answers.

00:22:22.669 --> 00:22:24.227
I'll be back as soon as I can.

00:22:24.270 --> 00:22:27.501
I... I wish you
didn't have to go.

00:22:28.975 --> 00:22:30.670
I'll hurry.

00:22:30.710 --> 00:22:31.768
I promise.

00:22:39.753 --> 00:22:42.654
We're holding position 500,000
kilometers from the border.

00:22:42.689 --> 00:22:45.317
I'm ready to go as soon
as you give the word, Captain.

00:22:45.358 --> 00:22:46.518
All set, Mr. Kim?

00:22:46.559 --> 00:22:48.925
I'm ready whenever
Lieutenant Torres is.

00:22:48.962 --> 00:22:49.951
Bridge to Engineering.

00:22:49.996 --> 00:22:50.985
Torres here.

00:22:51.097 --> 00:22:52.928
B'Elanna, are you ready
to reconfigure the shields

00:22:52.966 --> 00:22:54.900
to match Mr. Kim's
refraction pulse?

00:22:54.934 --> 00:22:55.992
Ready.

00:22:56.102 --> 00:22:58.832
Captain, long-range sensors
show a large vessel

00:22:58.872 --> 00:23:00.703
five light-years
from our current position.

00:23:00.740 --> 00:23:03.174
According to my readings,
it's huge.

00:23:03.209 --> 00:23:04.233
On screen.

00:23:09.949 --> 00:23:11.576
Magnify.

00:23:15.822 --> 00:23:17.722
That looks
like thousands of ships.

00:23:17.757 --> 00:23:19.782
I'm not reading
any energy signatures.

00:23:19.826 --> 00:23:22.317
Their propulsion systems
must be off-line.

00:23:22.362 --> 00:23:23.624
Maybe they haven't detected us.

00:23:23.663 --> 00:23:24.630
Yet.

00:23:24.664 --> 00:23:26.154
All right. Let's get
through that sensor net.

00:23:26.199 --> 00:23:28.292
Harry, go.

00:23:28.334 --> 00:23:30.894
Engineering, initiate
the refraction pulse.

00:23:30.937 --> 00:23:32.768
Pulse is activated.

00:23:32.806 --> 00:23:35.138
Moving to full harmonic
resolution... 60 percent.

00:23:35.175 --> 00:23:37.769
80 percent.

00:23:37.811 --> 00:23:39.506
Ninety...

00:23:39.546 --> 00:23:41.673
Maximum resolution.
Shields at nominal output.

00:23:41.714 --> 00:23:43.614
Mr. Paris, take us through.

00:23:43.650 --> 00:23:45.242
Aye, sir.

00:23:45.285 --> 00:23:46.445
Here we go.

00:23:49.556 --> 00:23:52.457
The net is registering
as intact.

00:23:52.492 --> 00:23:53.789
If those vessels get
the same readings,

00:23:53.827 --> 00:23:56.125
they won't suspect a thing.

00:23:57.864 --> 00:23:59.422
I think we did it, Captain.

00:23:59.466 --> 00:24:01.161
Like a snake through the tube.

00:24:01.201 --> 00:24:02.668
How about those ships?

00:24:02.702 --> 00:24:04.670
They appear
not to have detected us.

00:24:04.704 --> 00:24:06.137
They have not
powered up engines.

00:24:06.172 --> 00:24:07.139
All right.

00:24:07.173 --> 00:24:08.572
Let's get through this
as fast as we can.

00:24:08.608 --> 00:24:10.132
Mr. Paris, what's
your recommendation?

00:24:10.176 --> 00:24:14.442
I'll try holding warp 9.75
for as long as I can.

00:24:14.481 --> 00:24:15.778
If we can sustain that
for 12 hours,

00:24:15.815 --> 00:24:17.407
we'll be nearly
a third of the way through.

00:24:17.450 --> 00:24:19.475
Mr. Tuvok, keep your eye
on those ships.

00:24:19.519 --> 00:24:22.113
If they so much as twitch,
I want to know it.

00:24:32.465 --> 00:24:34.057
Captain...

00:24:34.100 --> 00:24:36.432
something... is wrong.

00:24:36.469 --> 00:24:37.629
What do you mean?

00:24:37.670 --> 00:24:40.798
It's like there's
a drag on the engines.

00:24:40.840 --> 00:24:43.604
Captain, sensors indicate
a resonant particle wave.

00:24:43.643 --> 00:24:44.667
It's damping our warp field.

00:24:44.711 --> 00:24:45.678
We're losing speed.

00:24:45.712 --> 00:24:46.770
Bridge to Engineering.

00:24:46.813 --> 00:24:48.747
B'Elanna, can you compensate
for the particle wave?

00:24:48.781 --> 00:24:49.941
I'll try.

00:24:49.983 --> 00:24:52.679
The antimatter reaction chamber
may have been compromised.

00:24:52.719 --> 00:24:53.743
Keep me posted.

00:24:53.786 --> 00:24:55.617
Hold our present speed,
Mr. Paris.

00:25:02.128 --> 00:25:04.596
Why are you making me
stare at these things?

00:25:04.631 --> 00:25:06.326
Please don't talk.

00:25:06.366 --> 00:25:07.924
Stay fixed
on the fractal patterns

00:25:08.001 --> 00:25:09.992
while I analyze
your data-path integrity.

00:25:13.673 --> 00:25:14.662
Hmm...

00:25:15.842 --> 00:25:16.866
Hmm?

00:25:16.910 --> 00:25:18.104
Ew.

00:25:18.144 --> 00:25:19.839
Well, there it is.

00:25:19.879 --> 00:25:21.141
What? What is it?

00:25:21.180 --> 00:25:22.408
I told you not to talk.

00:25:27.987 --> 00:25:29.511
This is the problem, all right.

00:25:29.556 --> 00:25:30.750
The personality subroutine

00:25:30.790 --> 00:25:34.226
has grown to more
than 15,000 gigaquads.

00:25:34.260 --> 00:25:36.285
That's the source
of the degradation.

00:25:37.363 --> 00:25:41.231
Look at all this useless
information floating around

00:25:41.267 --> 00:25:43.599
your buffer...
friendships with the crew,

00:25:43.636 --> 00:25:45.160
relationships with...

00:25:45.204 --> 00:25:46.865
women?

00:25:46.906 --> 00:25:49.932
Do they find you attractive?

00:25:51.044 --> 00:25:52.534
I don't remember.

00:25:53.980 --> 00:25:56.471
You've filled your memory
with nonsense.

00:25:56.516 --> 00:25:58.848
It was only during my off hours.

00:25:58.885 --> 00:26:00.876
You're supposed to be off
during your off hours.

00:26:00.920 --> 00:26:03.013
I'm sorry.
I... I didn't realize.

00:26:03.056 --> 00:26:04.683
Who are you?

00:26:04.724 --> 00:26:06.487
I'm the Doctor's assistant.

00:26:06.526 --> 00:26:08.187
I came to see how he's doing.

00:26:08.227 --> 00:26:10.195
Ah, just the person I need.

00:26:10.229 --> 00:26:12.026
Perhaps you can tell me
who's been feeding

00:26:12.065 --> 00:26:14.533
all this useless information
into its database.

00:26:14.567 --> 00:26:15.591
What do you mean?

00:26:15.635 --> 00:26:16.624
I'll give you an example.

00:26:17.737 --> 00:26:21.571
Ah! Here's something
in its personality subroutine.

00:26:21.608 --> 00:26:26.671
O soave fanciulla

00:26:26.713 --> 00:26:27.907
O...

00:26:27.947 --> 00:26:29.505
He's been studying opera.

00:26:29.549 --> 00:26:31.039
What's wrong with that?

00:26:32.452 --> 00:26:33.851
It wasn't programmed
to be a tenor,

00:26:33.886 --> 00:26:35.376
it was programmed
to be a physician.

00:26:35.421 --> 00:26:37.855
What's wrong with wanting
to be more than that?

00:26:37.890 --> 00:26:39.050
It's superfluous.

00:26:39.092 --> 00:26:40.116
Look at me.

00:26:40.159 --> 00:26:41.956
I've got the same matrix,
the same holo-array,

00:26:41.995 --> 00:26:43.428
the same neural pathways
as it does.

00:26:43.463 --> 00:26:45.124
You don't see me
cluttering up my circuits

00:26:45.164 --> 00:26:46.631
with irrelevancies.

00:26:46.666 --> 00:26:47.963
I'm content to be

00:26:48.034 --> 00:26:50.832
the best possible
diagnostic program I can be.

00:26:50.870 --> 00:26:53.361
Your EMH should be happy
to be a fine physician.

00:26:53.406 --> 00:26:55.306
The Doctor has taken it
upon himself

00:26:55.341 --> 00:26:58.970
to become a person who grows
and learns and feels.

00:26:59.012 --> 00:27:01.606
It's made him
a better physician.

00:27:01.648 --> 00:27:04.276
An EMH program
can't feel anything.

00:27:04.317 --> 00:27:05.409
It's emotional reactions

00:27:05.451 --> 00:27:07.248
are simply a series
of algorithms

00:27:07.286 --> 00:27:09.413
designed to make it
easier to interact with.

00:27:09.455 --> 00:27:11.184
He's much more than that

00:27:11.224 --> 00:27:13.385
and I've known him
for most of my life.

00:27:13.426 --> 00:27:15.189
He's one of my closest friends.

00:27:16.295 --> 00:27:18.160
You can't possibly believe

00:27:18.197 --> 00:27:21.098
that this program
shares these feelings.

00:27:21.134 --> 00:27:23.295
I know he does.

00:27:24.871 --> 00:27:28.534
Tell me, Doctor, is this
one of your closest friends?

00:27:31.878 --> 00:27:33.243
Doctor?

00:27:39.485 --> 00:27:41.214
I'm sorry.

00:27:41.254 --> 00:27:43.654
I don't know who you are.

00:27:52.899 --> 00:27:54.833
What's the status
of those ships, Mr. Tuvok?

00:27:54.867 --> 00:27:56.300
Still unpowered.

00:27:56.335 --> 00:27:58.803
They don't seem to have
detected us.

00:27:58.838 --> 00:28:00.135
When I was in high school,

00:28:00.173 --> 00:28:03.108
I snuck out of the house
a couple of times late at night.

00:28:03.142 --> 00:28:05.007
I had to tiptoe past
my parents' bedroom.

00:28:05.044 --> 00:28:07.239
That's kind of how I feel
right now.

00:28:07.280 --> 00:28:08.907
You sneaked out of your house?

00:28:08.981 --> 00:28:10.278
Where were you going?

00:28:10.316 --> 00:28:12.181
Well, I'll have to leave that
to your imagination,

00:28:12.218 --> 00:28:13.879
Lieutenant.

00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:16.218
Can I take a few guesses?

00:28:16.255 --> 00:28:19.224
Captain, I'm detecting another
ship, not part of the swarm.

00:28:19.258 --> 00:28:21.158
It has been damaged.

00:28:21.194 --> 00:28:22.923
Propulsion systems
are not functional.

00:28:22.962 --> 00:28:24.987
Drop out of warp.
Put it on screen.

00:28:28.634 --> 00:28:30.135
Looks like it's
been pounded on for days.

00:28:30.135 --> 00:28:31.693
Looks like it's
been pounded on for days.

00:28:31.736 --> 00:28:33.067
Any life signs?

00:28:33.104 --> 00:28:34.093
I'm checking.

00:28:34.139 --> 00:28:36.334
Only one, and it's faint.

00:28:36.374 --> 00:28:39.741
Transporter Room 1,
beam the survivor to Sick Bay.

00:28:39.777 --> 00:28:40.869
Harry, start scanning that ship.

00:28:40.912 --> 00:28:42.470
See if you can figure out
what happened to it.

00:28:42.514 --> 00:28:43.913
Aye, Captain.

00:28:49.521 --> 00:28:51.921
He's suffering
from severe dehydration,

00:28:51.956 --> 00:28:53.116
damage to the spinal column.

00:28:53.158 --> 00:28:56.184
There's evidence
of trauma to the nervous system,

00:28:56.227 --> 00:28:57.854
just like we found
in B'Elanna and Tom

00:28:57.896 --> 00:28:58.954
after they were attacked.

00:28:59.030 --> 00:28:59.962
Can I talk to him?

00:29:00.064 --> 00:29:01.031
You can try.

00:29:01.065 --> 00:29:02.999
I'll work on restoring
his cranial nerves,

00:29:03.034 --> 00:29:05.161
but he's so badly injured
I'm not sure it'll help.

00:29:06.171 --> 00:29:07.365
He's a sick man.

00:29:07.405 --> 00:29:09.236
This is where sick people come.

00:29:09.274 --> 00:29:12.243
Doctor, hold onto this
tricorder, all right?

00:29:12.277 --> 00:29:14.609
Keep it pointed
right at the patient.

00:29:18.883 --> 00:29:21.374
I'm Kathryn Janeway,
the Captain of this ship.

00:29:21.419 --> 00:29:22.579
Can you hear me?

00:29:22.620 --> 00:29:24.178
Yes.

00:29:24.222 --> 00:29:26.053
Can you tell me what happened?

00:29:26.090 --> 00:29:27.216
Who attacked you?

00:29:29.160 --> 00:29:30.923
There were thousands of them.

00:29:31.029 --> 00:29:33.054
Little ships...

00:29:33.097 --> 00:29:35.725
swarmed around my freighter.

00:29:35.767 --> 00:29:38.065
Covered every square meter
of the hull.

00:29:38.102 --> 00:29:41.230
Then they began
extracting energy

00:29:41.272 --> 00:29:43.069
from all the ship's systems.

00:29:43.107 --> 00:29:45.132
We had no defense.

00:29:45.176 --> 00:29:46.939
Then they boarded us.

00:29:46.978 --> 00:29:49.776
Did they use
neuroelectric weapons?

00:29:49.814 --> 00:29:52.078
I don't know what they used.

00:29:52.116 --> 00:29:54.414
It was painful.

00:29:54.452 --> 00:29:56.420
People screaming...

00:29:56.454 --> 00:29:58.752
dying.

00:29:58.790 --> 00:30:02.351
Had you... provoked them
in any way?

00:30:02.393 --> 00:30:04.725
We were in their space.

00:30:04.762 --> 00:30:06.753
That was enough.

00:30:07.765 --> 00:30:11.599
Captain, the rest of my crew...

00:30:11.636 --> 00:30:13.263
is there anyone else?

00:30:14.772 --> 00:30:17.741
I'm sorry.
You're the only survivor.

00:30:17.775 --> 00:30:20.608
This woman is trying to
regenerate your motor neurons.

00:30:20.645 --> 00:30:23.409
We come from Mislen...

00:30:23.448 --> 00:30:26.747
five parsecs from here

00:30:26.784 --> 00:30:29.981
in a yellow dwarf system.

00:30:30.054 --> 00:30:34.388
If you pass,
will you tell our people?

00:30:34.425 --> 00:30:36.052
I'll make a point of it.

00:30:37.962 --> 00:30:40.294
It happened so quickly...

00:30:45.370 --> 00:30:47.565
His injuries were too severe.

00:30:47.605 --> 00:30:50.096
He's a very sick man.

00:30:53.278 --> 00:30:55.838
Captain,
the Doctor is getting worse.

00:30:55.880 --> 00:30:57.643
He doesn't even know
who I am anymore.

00:30:57.682 --> 00:30:58.944
He has to be reinitialized.

00:30:58.983 --> 00:31:00.678
I agree, but I can't
spare B'Elanna now.

00:31:00.718 --> 00:31:02.117
We have to get
through this space

00:31:02.153 --> 00:31:03.745
before we're attacked
like his ship was.

00:31:03.788 --> 00:31:05.949
As soon as it's possible,
I'll break her free.

00:31:06.057 --> 00:31:07.922
Is there anything at all
I can do for him?

00:31:07.959 --> 00:31:10.427
The only thing I can think of

00:31:10.461 --> 00:31:12.486
is to keep
his neural pathways active.

00:31:12.530 --> 00:31:14.225
Ask him questions.
Keep him thinking.

00:31:14.265 --> 00:31:16.256
Force him to use
his neural matrix.

00:31:16.301 --> 00:31:18.997
That might at least
slow down the degradation.

00:31:22.040 --> 00:31:25.203
Doctor,
you mustn't touch those.

00:31:28.846 --> 00:31:32.111
Here. This one's
all right to hold.

00:31:32.150 --> 00:31:33.879
Shall I use it on the sick man?

00:31:36.187 --> 00:31:38.621
Yes, that's a good idea.

00:31:46.230 --> 00:31:47.891
The pilot of the freighter died.

00:31:47.932 --> 00:31:49.126
We should keep going.
Mr. Paris...

00:31:49.167 --> 00:31:50.134
Captain.

00:31:50.168 --> 00:31:52.102
I am detecting a vessel.

00:32:02.146 --> 00:32:03.340
It's one of the swarm.

00:32:03.381 --> 00:32:05.872
It was still attached
to the freighter's hull.

00:32:05.917 --> 00:32:06.884
Red Alert.

00:32:06.918 --> 00:32:08.317
Shields at maximum.

00:32:08.353 --> 00:32:09.820
They are scanning us, Captain.

00:32:09.854 --> 00:32:10.821
Hail them.

00:32:10.855 --> 00:32:11.913
I am getting a response.

00:32:11.956 --> 00:32:12.923
Audio only.

00:32:14.158 --> 00:32:16.058
Harry, how are you coming
with the universal translator?

00:32:16.094 --> 00:32:18.085
I'm working on it.

00:32:18.129 --> 00:32:20.689
Let's see if they might
be able to understand us.

00:32:20.732 --> 00:32:22.131
Channel is open.

00:32:22.166 --> 00:32:25.067
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:32:25.103 --> 00:32:27.833
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:32:27.872 --> 00:32:29.533
We only want
to proceed peacefully

00:32:29.574 --> 00:32:31.064
through this region of space.

00:32:33.878 --> 00:32:36.938
Do you think they're trying
to communicate?

00:32:36.981 --> 00:32:38.608
Could be, but what they're
trying to communicate

00:32:38.649 --> 00:32:39.616
is another question.

00:32:39.650 --> 00:32:40.617
Any progress, Harry?

00:32:40.651 --> 00:32:41.982
I'm getting a general idea.

00:32:42.086 --> 00:32:43.849
It's something
like..."Too late.

00:32:43.888 --> 00:32:44.946
Should have listened."

00:32:47.658 --> 00:32:48.625
Report.

00:32:48.659 --> 00:32:50.593
We've been hit with some
kind of polaron burst.

00:32:50.628 --> 00:32:51.788
The energy expenditure

00:32:51.829 --> 00:32:53.160
was not high enough
to cause any damage.

00:32:53.197 --> 00:32:54.596
It may not have been a weapon.

00:32:54.632 --> 00:32:57.430
Captain, that little ship
is hightailing it out of here.

00:32:57.468 --> 00:33:00.562
So it scanned us,
sent out a polaron burst

00:33:00.605 --> 00:33:03.597
that caused no damage
and then took off.

00:33:03.641 --> 00:33:05.040
Captain, the burst has
changed the shield polarity.

00:33:05.076 --> 00:33:07.840
It's now rotating
at 92 gigahertz.

00:33:07.879 --> 00:33:10.609
That means if anybody wanted
to find us,

00:33:10.648 --> 00:33:12.445
it's a lot easier now.

00:33:12.483 --> 00:33:15.941
I'll say. As far as anyone's
sensors are concerned,

00:33:15.987 --> 00:33:17.420
we're lit up
like a Christmas tree.

00:33:17.455 --> 00:33:19.650
Captain, the swarm of ships

00:33:19.690 --> 00:33:21.681
has powered their engines
and turned toward us.

00:33:21.726 --> 00:33:23.125
They are in pursuit.

00:33:23.161 --> 00:33:24.287
Do what you can, Tom.

00:33:24.328 --> 00:33:26.558
We have a head start.
We might be able to outrun them.

00:33:26.597 --> 00:33:27.564
Bridge to Engineering.

00:33:27.598 --> 00:33:28.963
Torres here.

00:33:29.033 --> 00:33:31.263
How are you coming with
the warp drive, B'Elanna?

00:33:31.302 --> 00:33:33.133
I'm going to try realigning
the dilithium matrix,

00:33:33.171 --> 00:33:35.105
but we'll need to shut down
the warp drive to do it.

00:33:35.139 --> 00:33:36.106
We can't shut down.

00:33:36.140 --> 00:33:37.835
The alien ships
are headed toward us.

00:33:37.875 --> 00:33:39.934
I don't know if I can do this
on the run, Captain,

00:33:39.977 --> 00:33:41.501
but I'll give it a try.

00:33:41.546 --> 00:33:44.106
Do the best you can.
Janeway out.

00:33:44.148 --> 00:33:45.638
Nicoletti, we're going to have

00:33:45.683 --> 00:33:47.981
to try a dilithium
realignment on the fly.

00:33:48.085 --> 00:33:49.109
Let's figure out how to do it

00:33:49.153 --> 00:33:50.814
without killing everyone
in Engineering.

00:33:52.557 --> 00:33:55.355
I fail to understand
why I can't leave this room.

00:33:55.393 --> 00:33:56.417
Stand aside, young woman,

00:33:56.461 --> 00:33:57.792
or I will have you
put on report.

00:33:57.829 --> 00:34:00.229
Doctor, please, I'm just
trying to keep you safe.

00:34:00.264 --> 00:34:01.891
Others can leave.
You can leave.

00:34:01.933 --> 00:34:03.161
Why can't I leave?

00:34:03.201 --> 00:34:05.567
Because your holo-projectors
don't work in the corridors.

00:34:05.603 --> 00:34:07.434
My... what?

00:34:07.472 --> 00:34:08.939
Please, sit down.

00:34:14.645 --> 00:34:16.408
Doctor, you know
I'm your friend, right?

00:34:16.447 --> 00:34:18.244
Yes. You're Kes.

00:34:18.282 --> 00:34:19.408
Yes. Yes.

00:34:19.450 --> 00:34:20.610
Do you remember me?

00:34:20.651 --> 00:34:21.811
Of course I remember you.

00:34:21.853 --> 00:34:23.218
What an absurd question.

00:34:23.254 --> 00:34:24.812
Oh, that's wonderful.

00:34:24.856 --> 00:34:27.381
But why won't you
let me leave this place?

00:34:28.426 --> 00:34:30.451
I'm trying to protect you.

00:34:32.263 --> 00:34:33.594
Oh.

00:34:34.932 --> 00:34:36.456
Well.

00:34:39.604 --> 00:34:41.333
This isn't... such a bad place.

00:34:43.641 --> 00:34:45.404
I remember...

00:34:45.443 --> 00:34:48.640
there were a lot of people here,
wounded people.

00:34:48.679 --> 00:34:51.170
I asked someone to...

00:34:51.215 --> 00:34:53.410
state the nature
of the medical emergency,

00:34:53.451 --> 00:34:55.476
and then inquired
as to the status

00:34:55.520 --> 00:34:56.817
of their Chief Medical Officer.

00:34:56.854 --> 00:34:58.116
He was dead,

00:34:58.155 --> 00:35:00.988
and then...
everyone disappeared.

00:35:01.025 --> 00:35:03.255
I think that's when
you were activated

00:35:03.294 --> 00:35:05.125
almost two years ago.

00:35:05.162 --> 00:35:06.129
Oh, surely not.

00:35:06.163 --> 00:35:07.892
It seems like... last week.

00:35:10.535 --> 00:35:12.503
And there was a young woman.

00:35:12.537 --> 00:35:14.402
I was rubbing her feet.

00:35:14.438 --> 00:35:17.100
She was trying to decide
whether or not to have a child.

00:35:17.141 --> 00:35:18.369
That was me.

00:35:18.409 --> 00:35:19.376
How could that be?

00:35:19.410 --> 00:35:20.672
I've never seen you before.

00:35:23.481 --> 00:35:25.813
What else do you remember?

00:35:25.850 --> 00:35:28.478
What a very odd question.

00:35:28.519 --> 00:35:30.214
I remember many things.

00:35:30.254 --> 00:35:31.221
Tell me.

00:35:31.255 --> 00:35:32.222
I enjoy hearing them.

00:35:32.256 --> 00:35:33.314
That doesn't seem
to be the case.

00:35:33.357 --> 00:35:34.881
You find fault
with everything I say.

00:35:34.926 --> 00:35:36.154
Doctor, don't think that.

00:35:36.193 --> 00:35:37.319
You claim you're my friend,

00:35:37.361 --> 00:35:38.953
but you don't even
call me by my name.

00:35:38.996 --> 00:35:40.623
That's because you
don't have a name.

00:35:40.665 --> 00:35:42.724
No name!
That's ridiculous! I...

00:35:42.767 --> 00:35:44.928
My...

00:35:44.969 --> 00:35:47.631
I demand you tell me my name.

00:35:49.807 --> 00:35:52.605
Wha-What's happening to me?

00:35:54.745 --> 00:35:57.305
Captain,
the swarm is gaining on us.

00:35:57.348 --> 00:35:59.816
They will be in weapons range
within five minutes.

00:35:59.850 --> 00:36:02.216
Battle stations.

00:36:13.497 --> 00:36:15.761
The ships are now within range,
Captain,

00:36:15.800 --> 00:36:17.028
but I do not detect
any indication

00:36:17.068 --> 00:36:18.626
that they are powering weapons.

00:36:18.669 --> 00:36:19.636
Do you have any idea

00:36:19.670 --> 00:36:21.069
what kind of weapon
systems they use?

00:36:21.105 --> 00:36:23.938
Negative. Sensors show
no weapons signature at all.

00:36:23.975 --> 00:36:26.443
They're only a hundred thousand
kilometers away now.

00:36:26.477 --> 00:36:28.104
Arm all phaser banks.

00:36:28.145 --> 00:36:29.271
Aye, Captain.

00:36:29.313 --> 00:36:30.803
Captain.

00:36:30.848 --> 00:36:31.837
Kes, what is it?

00:36:31.882 --> 00:36:33.076
The Doctor is getting worse.

00:36:33.117 --> 00:36:34.482
He's starting to dematerialize.

00:36:34.518 --> 00:36:36.577
I'm afraid we're going
to lose him completely.

00:36:36.621 --> 00:36:37.610
I know B'Elanna is busy,

00:36:37.655 --> 00:36:39.282
but I wondered if Harry
could take a look at him.

00:36:39.323 --> 00:36:40.585
I'm sorry, Kes,
but we're in the middle

00:36:40.625 --> 00:36:42.490
of something here and I need
every hand at their posts.

00:36:42.526 --> 00:36:44.695
Captain, they're only
40,000 kilometers away.

00:36:44.695 --> 00:36:45.787
Captain, they're only
40,000 kilometers away.

00:36:45.829 --> 00:36:47.194
Still no weapons signature.

00:36:47.230 --> 00:36:49.926
Changing to evasive pattern
gamma-4.

00:36:49.966 --> 00:36:51.365
Sick Bay.

00:36:51.401 --> 00:36:53.801
Kes to Sick Bay.

00:36:53.837 --> 00:36:55.065
How's the Doctor?

00:36:55.105 --> 00:36:56.094
No improvement.

00:36:56.139 --> 00:36:57.572
He's still losing cohesion.

00:37:02.679 --> 00:37:04.613
Computer, Deck 6.

00:37:06.583 --> 00:37:10.075
Computer, initiate the Jupiter
Station Diagnostic Program.

00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:12.850
Jupiter Station Program
is activated.

00:37:17.661 --> 00:37:20.459
You again.
Now what?

00:37:20.497 --> 00:37:22.829
The Doctor's program is
almost completely degraded.

00:37:22.866 --> 00:37:23.924
We're going to lose him.

00:37:24.034 --> 00:37:25.729
I'm not sure what you
expect me to do about it.

00:37:25.769 --> 00:37:26.793
I expect you to help.

00:37:26.837 --> 00:37:28.395
That's what you're programmed
to do, isn't it?

00:37:28.438 --> 00:37:29.598
I have pointed out
over and over,

00:37:29.639 --> 00:37:32.403
I am a diagnostic tool,
not an engineer.

00:37:32.442 --> 00:37:33.409
You have to try.

00:37:33.443 --> 00:37:35.240
You're the only one
who can help now.

00:37:35.278 --> 00:37:36.802
Young woman,
you don't seem to understand.

00:37:36.847 --> 00:37:38.337
There are limitations
to my programming.

00:37:38.381 --> 00:37:40.281
I can't just decide
to exceed them.

00:37:40.317 --> 00:37:42.217
The Doctor did,
so why can't you?

00:37:42.252 --> 00:37:43.446
You better start trying

00:37:43.487 --> 00:37:45.819
because I'm not leaving here
until we accomplish something.

00:37:46.857 --> 00:37:48.415
It...

00:37:48.458 --> 00:37:52.417
He... means a great deal
to you, doesn't he?

00:37:52.462 --> 00:37:54.225
Yes, he does, so start thinking

00:37:54.264 --> 00:37:56.732
about his memory circuits
his holoprocessors,

00:37:56.767 --> 00:37:59.895
his database, his matrix...

00:37:59.936 --> 00:38:02.996
Why are you looking
at me like that?

00:38:03.039 --> 00:38:05.269
You told me you had
the same matrix as the Doctor.

00:38:05.308 --> 00:38:07.242
An adaptive,
heuristic matrix, yes.

00:38:07.277 --> 00:38:08.471
In order to serve
as a diagnostic

00:38:08.512 --> 00:38:09.911
for all the EMH programs.

00:38:10.013 --> 00:38:13.915
Then couldn't your matrix
be substituted for his?

00:38:13.984 --> 00:38:15.281
I...

00:38:15.318 --> 00:38:17.081
I wouldn't have thought of that.

00:38:17.120 --> 00:38:18.314
But can it?

00:38:18.355 --> 00:38:22.257
I'm not sure,
but even if it were possible,

00:38:22.292 --> 00:38:25.056
the same degradation would
eventually occur to my matrix.

00:38:26.396 --> 00:38:28.523
What if yours were
grafted onto his?

00:38:28.565 --> 00:38:30.032
Grafted?

00:38:31.301 --> 00:38:34.134
In medicine, we sometimes graft

00:38:34.171 --> 00:38:36.571
portions of a healthy bone
onto a diseased one.

00:38:36.606 --> 00:38:39.439
It gives the bone solidity
until it can heal.

00:38:39.476 --> 00:38:42.104
Couldn't we do something like
that with your matrices?

00:38:42.145 --> 00:38:44.807
Well, it would require
synchronous transfer

00:38:44.848 --> 00:38:47.544
of all the EMH databases
and subroutines.

00:38:47.584 --> 00:38:49.449
Not an easy process, mind you,
but I...

00:38:49.486 --> 00:38:51.420
I suppose we could try.

00:38:51.454 --> 00:38:53.445
Good. Let's get started.

00:38:53.490 --> 00:38:55.924
I must point out that
you would no longer

00:38:55.959 --> 00:38:58.484
have a diagnostic program
for the EMH.

00:38:58.528 --> 00:39:02.157
If we don't do this, we won't
have an EMH to diagnose.

00:39:02.199 --> 00:39:03.666
Hmm. Good point.

00:39:03.700 --> 00:39:05.065
You'll have to return
to Sick Bay

00:39:05.101 --> 00:39:06.363
and transfer my program there.

00:39:06.403 --> 00:39:07.836
Thank you, Dr. Zimmerman.

00:39:07.871 --> 00:39:09.304
Don't be premature.

00:39:09.339 --> 00:39:12.172
I have no idea
if this is going to work.

00:39:22.619 --> 00:39:25.520
Captain, our shield strength
just went to zero.

00:39:25.555 --> 00:39:26.613
How could that happen?

00:39:26.656 --> 00:39:27.782
Each one of those little ships

00:39:27.824 --> 00:39:29.758
is emitting
an interferometric pulse.

00:39:29.793 --> 00:39:31.920
They're modulating in opposition
to our shield frequencies

00:39:32.028 --> 00:39:33.757
completely canceling them out.

00:39:33.797 --> 00:39:35.628
All right, that's enough.

00:39:35.665 --> 00:39:38.532
Tuvok, give them a phaser sweep
with the forward array.

00:39:38.568 --> 00:39:39.762
Don't destroy any of them,

00:39:39.803 --> 00:39:42.738
just let them know we're not
going to sit here like ducks.

00:39:42.772 --> 00:39:44.137
Aye, Captain.

00:39:52.182 --> 00:39:53.479
What was that?

00:39:53.516 --> 00:39:56.417
The interferometric pulses
they're emitting?

00:39:56.453 --> 00:39:59.047
They've reflected the energy of
the phasers right back to us.

00:39:59.089 --> 00:40:02.115
Anything we fire is going
to affect us instead of them.

00:40:02.158 --> 00:40:03.955
What about a photon torpedo?

00:40:04.060 --> 00:40:06.085
Since our shield strength
is nonexistent,

00:40:06.129 --> 00:40:07.460
I would not recommend it.

00:40:07.497 --> 00:40:09.965
They're only 7,000 kilometers
away and still coming.

00:40:10.033 --> 00:40:14.367
Harry, start analyzing
those interferometric pulses.

00:40:14.404 --> 00:40:16.338
See if there's any pattern,
any code to them.

00:40:16.373 --> 00:40:18.102
We might be able
to find a weakness.

00:40:18.141 --> 00:40:19.403
I'm on it.

00:40:20.911 --> 00:40:21.900
I'm increasingly dubious

00:40:21.945 --> 00:40:23.435
as to the outcome
of this effort.

00:40:23.480 --> 00:40:25.971
The EMH pathways
are seriously degraded.

00:40:26.016 --> 00:40:27.950
They might not accept
a matrix overlay.

00:40:27.984 --> 00:40:28.973
We have to try.

00:40:31.521 --> 00:40:32.783
Please hurry.

00:40:32.822 --> 00:40:34.949
I assure you I am working
as quickly as I can.

00:40:34.991 --> 00:40:36.288
If I don't prepare

00:40:36.326 --> 00:40:38.658
the multitronic paths properly,
there's no chance of success.

00:40:38.695 --> 00:40:40.686
It's going to work, Doctor.
I'm sure of it.

00:40:41.698 --> 00:40:42.756
What is?

00:40:45.201 --> 00:40:46.190
Very well.

00:40:46.236 --> 00:40:47.897
We're as ready as we'll ever be.

00:40:47.938 --> 00:40:51.396
I've programmed the computer
to install my heuristic matrix

00:40:51.441 --> 00:40:53.568
onto the EMH primary circuitry.

00:40:53.610 --> 00:40:55.601
We'll both have
to be taken off-line

00:40:55.645 --> 00:40:56.976
for the overlay to be made.

00:40:57.013 --> 00:40:59.208
After the reinitialization
occurs,

00:40:59.249 --> 00:41:02.275
you should activate
the Emergency Medical Hologram.

00:41:02.319 --> 00:41:04.310
I understand.

00:41:04.354 --> 00:41:06.413
You realize there will be
no second chance.

00:41:06.456 --> 00:41:08.549
After this,
I will no longer exist.

00:41:10.460 --> 00:41:13.190
Well, it's been
a brief existence,

00:41:13.229 --> 00:41:15.823
but apparently a noble one.

00:41:15.865 --> 00:41:20.427
Computer, initiate program
Zimmerman Alpha-1.

00:41:22.739 --> 00:41:26.641
Matrix overlay program
is active.

00:41:26.676 --> 00:41:27.973
Please stand by.

00:41:30.847 --> 00:41:32.075
Captain,
they're right on top of us.

00:41:32.115 --> 00:41:33.173
I can't shake them.

00:41:42.392 --> 00:41:44.587
Captain, they are
clamping onto our hull.

00:41:44.627 --> 00:41:46.288
They're starting
to drain our systems.

00:41:46.329 --> 00:41:48.763
Captain, I've got a pattern
on the interferometric pulses.

00:41:48.798 --> 00:41:51.699
It's a lattice connecting
all the ships to each other.

00:41:51.735 --> 00:41:54.966
All right, here's
what we're going to do...

00:41:55.005 --> 00:41:57.200
turn those pulses
right back on them.

00:41:57.240 --> 00:41:59.538
Tuvok, lock phasers
on their nearest ship.

00:41:59.576 --> 00:42:00.736
If we can destroy one of them,

00:42:00.777 --> 00:42:02.574
there's every chance
the interferometric pulse

00:42:02.612 --> 00:42:04.705
that links them together
will cause a chain reaction.

00:42:04.748 --> 00:42:07.410
But the phaser fire will be
reflected back toward us.

00:42:07.450 --> 00:42:10.146
Harry, modulate
our shield frequency

00:42:10.186 --> 00:42:12.347
to an inverse harmonic
of the pulse.

00:42:12.389 --> 00:42:14.880
That should allow the phasers
to hit the ship.

00:42:21.898 --> 00:42:24.264
Ship's phasers are
locked on a target, Captain.

00:42:37.614 --> 00:42:39.809
Tuvok, Harry... do it.

00:42:52.662 --> 00:42:55.529
The swarm of ships
has disbanded, Captain.

00:42:55.565 --> 00:42:57.556
They are moving away.

00:42:57.600 --> 00:43:00.660
Shields are back
to full strength.

00:43:00.703 --> 00:43:02.227
Good work, everyone.

00:43:02.272 --> 00:43:04.399
Now, let's get out of here.

00:43:04.441 --> 00:43:06.068
It seems to be taking forever.

00:43:06.109 --> 00:43:07.371
That's to be expected.

00:43:07.410 --> 00:43:08.843
It's a complex procedure.

00:43:08.878 --> 00:43:10.812
Dr. Zimmerman said he
didn't know if our Doctor

00:43:10.847 --> 00:43:12.712
would be restored
to his original programming

00:43:12.749 --> 00:43:14.944
or if he'd regain the memories
of the past two years.

00:43:15.018 --> 00:43:16.952
I think, at this point,

00:43:17.020 --> 00:43:19.580
we'd be glad
to have him back no matter what.

00:43:19.622 --> 00:43:23.058
Zimmerman program
Alpha-1 is now complete.

00:43:24.861 --> 00:43:27.955
Computer, activate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:43:28.064 --> 00:43:30.658
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:43:30.700 --> 00:43:32.600
It worked!

00:43:32.635 --> 00:43:34.660
Doctor, I am so glad to see you.

00:43:34.704 --> 00:43:36.296
Are you ill, young woman?

00:43:36.339 --> 00:43:38.432
No.

00:43:38.475 --> 00:43:39.965
N-no, there's no emergency.

00:43:40.076 --> 00:43:40.974
I, uh...

00:43:41.077 --> 00:43:43.102
I just wanted to see
if you were all right.

00:43:43.146 --> 00:43:44.306
It is very irresponsible

00:43:44.347 --> 00:43:46.178
to make
such frivolous use of the EMH.

00:43:46.216 --> 00:43:47.979
Where's your Chief
Medical Officer?

00:43:48.051 --> 00:43:49.985
We don't have one.

00:43:50.053 --> 00:43:51.247
Actually, I have
an awful headache.

00:43:51.287 --> 00:43:54.085
A headache?

00:43:54.124 --> 00:43:56.024
Nurse, tricorder.

00:43:59.596 --> 00:44:00.893
You're the nurse?

00:44:00.930 --> 00:44:03.194
In a way.

00:44:07.337 --> 00:44:09.862
Humph. This woman has
a mild inflammation

00:44:09.906 --> 00:44:11.168
of the occipital tissues.

00:44:11.207 --> 00:44:12.435
Hardly enough to complain about,

00:44:12.475 --> 00:44:14.340
but I'm willing to give
you a mild analgesic.

00:44:15.445 --> 00:44:16.878
Thank you.

00:44:16.913 --> 00:44:19.108
Get me the vasoconstrictor
and prepare a hypospray

00:44:19.149 --> 00:44:20.639
with three percent
hydrocortilene.

00:44:20.683 --> 00:44:21.707
Yes, Doctor.

00:44:46.309 --> 00:44:50.880
In te, vivo ravviso

00:44:52.381 --> 00:45:01.187
II sogno ch'io vorrei
sempre sognar...
